    { "dot": "cyan", "title": "Why this is continuous batching", "items": [
      "The scheduler runs every step, not once per batch",
      "A finished request frees its blocks inside update(), so the next step can admit",
      "Prefills and decodes share one forward pass (ragged query_lens)" ] },
    { "dot": "emerald", "title": "Two-phase cache use", "items": [
      "match() asks 'how much would this save?' without committing",
      "acquire() commits only once admission is certain",
